      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-03-10T16:32:32.493Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This is pretty cool – thanks for sharing! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=9\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\"></p>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/powerhound_2000\">@Powerhound_2000</a> : I read “Does the environment have threats?” as “Are there threats <em>defined</em> for this environment that can/should be introduced to the scene at this point?”, but I could have read it incorrectly! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/blush.png?v=9\" title=\":blush:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":blush:\"> (So not really “Are there environment threats that are currently active?”.)</p>\n<p>How did you intend it, <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/dr_flem\">@Dr_Flem</a> ? Maybe there’s a way to word it that would reflect that intention more closely?</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-03-10T16:33:02.498Z",
